{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>According to their birth.</b> Rashi explained: in the order [they were born]. Odem for Reuven, Pitdah for Shimon, and so all of them. And this does not seem correct to R. Tam, for according to the order of their birth, Leshem would not fall to Dan, since Dan is the fifth son of Jacob, and in the book of Joshua: ויקראו שם העיר לשם על שם דן אביהם. And it appears preferable to explain that 'in the order of their birth' means in the order of the birth of the mothers — all the sons of Leah first, and the sons of Bilhah after them, and the sons of Zilpah after them, and after them the sons of Rachel. And then you will find Leshem for Dan and Yashfeh for Binyamin, as the paytan established in the kerovetz for Purim: גלף מישפה תבנית. And in Sotah I found that it concludes the matter differently; it concludes in the chapter ואלו נאמרין: Rav Kahana said — just as they are divided here, i.e., on Mount Gerizim and on Mount Eival, so they are divided on the stones of the efod. For the High Priest had two efod stones on his shoulders, one on this side and one on that, and the names of the twelve tribes were written on them — six on this stone and six on that stone, as it is written: ששה משמותם etc. And the first stone is not 'according to their birth,' since Judah comes before [Issachar and Zebulun]. And it seems to me that regarding it [the second stone] it is written הנותרים — from which it follows that the first ones were not in the order of their birth. And it further concludes there: וחמשים אותיות הוי — twenty-five on this stone and twenty-five on that stone. Rabbi Hanina ben Gamliel says: not as they are divided here are they divided on the efod, but rather as they are divided in ואלה שמות — the sons of Leah in their order, the sons of Rachel in their order, one on this side and one on that, and the sons of the maidservants in the middle. Then how do I fulfill 'according to their birth'? — as the names their father called them, and not as the names Moses called them: ראובן and not ראובני, and so all of them. For 'according to their birth' refers only to the stones of the efod and not to the stones of the choshen, and to the first stone specifically and not to the second, as I have explained. תן לחכם ויחכם עוד."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {0 "The kerovetz for Purim containing the phrase גלף מישפה תבנית is a piyyut establishing the correspondence between the twelve tribes and the twelve stones. The closing line תן לחכם ויחכם עוד ('give to a wise man and he will grow wiser') is a traditional sign-off, not part of the exegetical argument."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:04:18.719214133Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}